From bbbc2053d4b51e5a67648f0f80ad32370f2068b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 10:21:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Peanuts Nova: Analyse for modding in place of Build
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The game sheet's Build and the game page's Prepare again / Build again
give way to "Analyser pour le modding": ModAnalysisService (in the :pack
process) runs dm/tools/fc27probe.py "all" in the packer's own Python on
the game's .nup where it is: the RomFS listing, every superbundle .toc
and every bundle manifest, read with one thread per core, into one zip
in Download/PeanutsNova-modding, with a progress notification. A game
without its pack offers Import pack… (packs come from Peanuts Native).
